# Chromebook additions, composed after omarchy-base.packages and
# omarchy-aarch64.packages (omarchy-pkg-defaults aarch64-chromebook): what
# every ARM Chromebook runs. The kernel comes with the Chromebook's image, as
# the kernel and bootloader do from the ISO on x86_64: each board's kernel is
# named by its device profile (book/devices/<codename>/kernel). What a
# Chromebook cannot boot or type without (the depthcharge tools, the ChromeOS
# keyboard map, the board's audio routing) comes as the platform packages'
# dependencies, so a new board needs no change here.

# The Chromebook's runtime and boot packages (book/packages).
omarchy-chromebook
omarchy-chromebook-boot
